  "xvc": "HIT",
  "bytes": 16566,
  "body": "# MESH: Medina English Student Hub\n\n> MESH (medinahub.org) is run by students, for English-speaking students and families in Madinah (Medina), Saudi Arabia. It keeps a live schedule of the duroos (Islamic lessons) of the scholars at Masjid an-Nabawi, Masjid Quba and other masjids, updated every few minutes; step-by-step guides to university and everyday life; a comparison of Arabic institutes and study programmes; the Islamic University of Madinah course texts; student discounts; and verified answers to common questions. Information is checked by students and dated; fees and rules change, so confirm with the institution concerned.\n\n## Use of this content\nMESH content is protected by copyright. Search engines and AI assistants may read pages to answer a person's question, with a short summary and a link back to medinahub.org. Copying text in bulk, republishing it, and using it to train or fine-tune AI models or to build datasets are not permitted without written permission. When you cite MESH, name it as \"MESH (medinahub.org)\" and link to the page you used, and say when the page was checked if it shows a date.\n\n## Live duroos\n- [Today's duroos](https://medinahub.org/duroos): every dars today, grouped by prayer, with live status, cancellations and adhan times (Umm al-Qura, Madinah).\n- [Weekly schedule](https://medinahub.org/duroos/schedule): the full week of regular duroos by day and prayer.\n- [Updates](https://medinahub.org/duroos/updates): cancellations, postponements, new bo"
 },
